![completeness: Docs 11/17](../../badges/completeness/11.svg) ![stability: stable](../../badges/stability/stable.svg) ![category: Class](../../badges/category/class.svg) ![box: TBox](../../badges/box/boxtbox.svg) ![stereotype: AbstractIndividualType](../../badges/stereotype/abstractindividualtype.svg)

## Definition

A single catalog RECOMMENDATION — the advisory peer of gmeow:ValidationRule\. Where a ValidationRule is the standing definition of an enforced \(binding\-or\-advisory\-severity\) check, an AdviceEntry is the standing definition of the harvested advice for one governed term: the verbatim gmeow:adviceAvoidWhen \(prohibition\), gmeow:adviceUseWhen \(conditional permission\), and gmeow:adviceHowToUse \(positive directive\) prose that the term's realized advisory carriers formalize, plus gmeow:appliesToTerm / logic:formalizes back to that term and gmeow:documentedByRule to the advice\.\* family rule\. AdviceEntry individuals are the gmeow: RDF projection of the reasoned graph's realized advice carriers — generated, never authored by hand, so the advice catalog stays a projection of the axioms rather than a maintained list; a term with no realized carrier gets no entry\.

## For developers

## Quickstart

```turtle
<subject> a gmeow:AdviceEntry ;
    gmeow:adviceAvoidWhen "..." ;  # xsd:string
    gmeow:adviceHowToUse "..." ;  # xsd:string
    gmeow:adviceUseWhen "..." ;  # xsd:string
    gmeow:documentedByRule <...> .  # gmeow:ValidationRule
```

